OL,3,GNEWSAExplosive wreck bookings surge
OL,4,Abefore mast removal
OL,5,
OL,6,FTour operators offering excursions to a
OL,7,FUS Liberty ship which sank in the
OL,8,FThames Estuary off the Kent coast say
OL,9,Fthat the number of bookings is
OL,10,Fincreasing ahead of its masts being
OL,11,Fremoved.
OL,13,FThe Department for Transport (DfT) has
OL,14,Fconfirmed work on the SS Richard
OL,15,FMontgomery will start in September
OL,16,Fafter plans drawn up in 2020 were
OL,17,Fdelayed.
OL,19,FEngineers will work underwater to cut
OL,20,Fthe masts off the World War Two
OL,21,Fshipwreck, which has 1,400 tonnes of
OL,22,Fexplosives on board.
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,322,320,200,140,0,100
